<!--
  The themed-icon layer (Android 13+), where the system keeps the alpha channel
  and throws the colour away. So the gorilla cannot be shaded here the way he is
  in ic_launcher_foreground: fur, face and muzzle all flatten into one opaque
  blob, and the head would come out as a plain circle with ears.

  He is drawn as a silhouette instead, with the eyes and the muzzle cut out of
  it rather than painted on. android:fillType="evenOdd" turns a subpath
  enclosed by another into a hole, and the nostrils, being enclosed in turn by
  the muzzle, flip back to solid and become islands inside it.

  Same group transform and the same skull outline as the foreground layer, so
  the two line up exactly. The features are not: the eyes are widened to 12 and
  the muzzle narrowed, because at the foreground's proportions the eyes read as
  pinpricks over a broad snout, which is a pig rather than an ape. The smile is
  dropped, being line work too fine to survive launcher size, and the nostrils
  with it: as islands in the muzzle they were most of what made it a snout.

  The brow is the one feature carried over unchanged, and it is the feature that
  does the work. Without it this is an anonymous round face with two dots; with
  it the icon still reads as a gorilla at 36px.

  evenOdd is why the ears are a separate path: they overlap the skull, and in a
  shared path that overlap would read as one-inside-the-other and punch a hole
  through each side of his head. Two opaque paths simply union instead.

  For the same reason no two holes may touch. They currently clear each other by
  8 units at the tightest (eyes to muzzle), and the brow's outer tips stop 2
  short of the ears; an overlap anywhere would flip back to solid and show up as
  a blot rather than as a gap.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="108dp"
    android:height="108dp"
    android:viewportWidth="108"
    android:viewportHeight="108">

    <group
        android:pivotX="100"
        android:pivotY="84"
        android:scaleX="0.42"
        android:scaleY="0.42"
        android:translateX="-46"
        android:translateY="-30">

        <path
            android:fillColor="#000000"
            android:pathData="M16,86 A17,19 0 1,1 50,86 A17,19 0 1,1 16,86 Z
                              M150,86 A17,19 0 1,1 184,86 A17,19 0 1,1 150,86 Z" />

        <path
            android:fillColor="#000000"
            android:fillType="evenOdd"
            android:pathData="M100,18 C143,18 166,46 166,86 C166,126 138,150 100,150
                              C62,150 34,126 34,86 C34,46 57,18 100,18 Z
                              M52,84 C60,66 78,58 100,58 C122,58 140,66 148,84
                              C138,74 122,70 100,70 C78,70 62,74 52,84 Z
                              M67,93 A12,12 0 1,1 91,93 A12,12 0 1,1 67,93 Z
                              M109,93 A12,12 0 1,1 133,93 A12,12 0 1,1 109,93 Z
                              M76,126 A24,13 0 1,1 124,126 A24,13 0 1,1 76,126 Z" />

    </group>

</vector>
